<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>DW - English for Africa</title><subtitle type="html">News, Analysis and Service from Germany and Europe - in 30 Languages</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa</id><updated>2026-10-16T19:37:53Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-africa" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-12756?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Ethiopia's Abiy Ahmed appoints interim Tigray government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:721fe8a45fcf717f9004acae78af61cf6ec3f2edf358a3aa17766aba58e8f64a</id><updated>2026-10-16T19:37:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T16:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ethiopia-s-abiy-ahmed-appoints-interim-tigray-government/a-79683519--c9a39db6c855.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ethiopia-s-abiy-ahmed-appoints-interim-tigray-government/a-79683519?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Abiy Ahmed's office said there would be elections held in Tigray within 6 months. The move comes after an escalation in fighting between federal forces and a rebel alliance.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>German colonialism on agenda in Bundestag debate on Namibia genocide</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c477e34308c700faf0daf5d419a9d9bf68c7d190824ad5c55afdacb0d9efc41c</id><updated>2026-10-16T19:37:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T14:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-colonialism-on-agenda-in-bundestag-debate-on-namibia-genocide/a-79682388--e473209aeb4e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-colonialism-on-agenda-in-bundestag-debate-on-namibia-genocide/a-79682388?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Opposition parties have forced a debate in the Bundestag on the early-20th-century genocide Germany carried out in Namibia. Will this finally spur progress in addressing colonial crimes?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>How prepared is Kenya for an Ebola outbreak?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c698796884b192d1d956ae33294a8b5c8ad8486b9a95ac8c5eaf71ca758e3c6e</id><updated>2026-10-16T19:36:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T10:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-prepared-is-kenya-for-an-ebola-outbreak/a-79668144--2b6e19c28555.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-prepared-is-kenya-for-an-ebola-outbreak/a-79668144?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The first two confirmed Ebola cases in Kenya have raised urgent questions about the country's public health preparedness and border controls. But the Health Ministry says there is no need for panic.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Formula One in Rwanda: Sportswashing claims vs. hopes for African legacy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e73819faf5fe5f0b16a7aae5f8ca919889f09adc4bba6b89abe76b490213684a</id><updated>2026-10-16T19:36:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T08:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/formula-one-in-rwanda-sportswashing-claims-vs-hopes-for-african-legacy/a-79650744--59b33a158fd3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/formula-one-in-rwanda-sportswashing-claims-vs-hopes-for-african-legacy/a-79650744?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Formula One will return to Africa for the first time since 1993. There is concern Rwanda are using it as another sportswashing opportunity, but there is also hope the event's legacy can impact wider African society.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry></feed>
